On 1/19/07, Anand Deopurkar <anand.deopurkar@gmail.com> wrote:
> Why do ba bo and pu bo mean opposites of what they should mean?

An unfortunate oversight by the designers.

> For example, la meris klama ba lenu mi klama fi le kumfa. (Mary came after I
> left the room)
> should be equivalent to - la meris klama .i babo mi klama le kumfa.

Yes. It wouldn't be much of a problem if all tags consistently behaved
that way, but unfortunately that's not the case. For example:
{la meris klama ki'u lenu mi klama fi le kumfa} is basically equivalent
to {la meris klama .i ki'u bo mi klama fi le kumfa}. So tense-tags and
BAI-tags don't behave the same way.

